    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense enters today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as the undisputed centerpiece. With a score of 75.30, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive park factor boost (+16%) and a favorable matchup against Woo, positioning him as the primary engine for Runs and HRs today. While **Kyle Tucker** (68.96) and **Andy Pages** (63.73) also grade out as strong starts against Keller, the aggressive deployment of **Gunnar Henderson** in the #2 hole maximizes his counting stat potential despite the 42% rain risk hovering over the contest. **Josh Jung** (60.61) rounds out our top-tier tier of starters; while he faces the crafty Wacha, the combination of a wind-aided environment and a clean #3 spot in the lineup elevates his efficiency above our baseline expectations.\n\nConversely, we are treading carefully at the bottom of the order. **Sam Antonacci** (44.84) and **Coby Mayo** (41.80) are firmly in the marginal category, salvaged only by our need to preserve game caps while maintaining positional utility. **Sam Antonacci**\u2019s poor ranking is exacerbated by a negative platoon split and a suboptimal #9 spot, while **Coby Mayo** is similarly hamstrung by batting eighth. **Liam Hicks** (57.76) and **Miguel Vargas** (58.80) represent our most stable floor plays; both are benefiting from solid SP_xERA matchups against Kelly and P\u00e9rez, respectively. With **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jordan Westburg** all sidelined by off-days or injuries, our bench remains thin, leaving little room for error if the weather in the Woo matchup forces an early game cancellation. If the rain intensifies, we will need to pivot to deeper bench options like **Heliot Ramos** or **Josh Lowe** to maintain our competitive edge in the scarcity-driven SB category.",
